<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-cherasco"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Cherasco</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1631</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Cherasco, signed in 1631 at Cherasco in Piedmont, ended the War of the Mantuan Succession.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-coche"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/treaty-of-coche.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Coche</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1863</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Coche was the agreement signed in April 1863 at the Coche estate near Caracas that ended the Federal War in Venezuela.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-concordia"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Concordia</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · 1648</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Concordia, signed on 23 March 1648, divided the Caribbean island of Saint Martin between France and the Dutch Republic after the Spanish garrison had left.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-constantinople-1700"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Constantinople (1700)</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1700</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Constantinople of July 1700 ended the war of 1686–1700 between Russia and the Ottoman Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-constantinople-1832"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/treaty-of-constantinople-1832.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Constantinople (1832)</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1832</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Constantinople was signed in July 1832 by Britain, France, Russia and the Ottoman Empire, completing the recognition of the independent Kingdom of Greece.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-copenhagen-1441"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Copenhagen (1441)</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1441</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Copenhagen of 1441 ended the naval war of 1438–1441 between the Wendish towns of the Hanseatic League, led by Lübeck, and Holland and Zeeland.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-copenhagen-1660"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Copenhagen (1660)</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1660</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Copenhagen was signed on 27 May 1660 between Denmark-Norway and Sweden, ending the war that Charles X Gustav had renewed in 1658.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-corbeil-1258"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Corbeil (1258)</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1258</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Corbeil was signed in May 1258 between Louis IX of France and James I of Aragon.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-cordoba"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/treaty-of-cordoba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Córdoba</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1821</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Córdoba was signed on 24 August 1821 at Córdoba, Veracruz, by Agustín de Iturbide and Juan O'Donojú, the last Spanish head of government of New Spain.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-daan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/treaty-of-daan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Treaty of Da'an</span><span class="enc-type">Treaty · Peace · 1911</span><span class="enc-snip">The Treaty of Da'an was an agreement concluded in 1911 at Da'an, north-west of Sanaa, between the Ottoman Empire and the Zaydi imam Ya